is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.1).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =0.1,$ and\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{0.1}\\,\\text{hours}=10\\,\\text{hours}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next smartphone is purchased is $10$ hours."} :step/id #uuid "034cf39f-21a0-52ca-b145-e27e4f9c0e99" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491264}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491229 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4821eb28-1e88-51ad-aad4-f7dfdfec6587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490646} {:answer/id #uuid "4a63109f-beee-5a5f-8861-1aea21eee120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490653} {:answer/id #uuid "4f92c2ad-9f48-554d-9500-741e357a8e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490665} {:answer/id #uuid "91460a8c-4330-566f-8171-430847261e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490805} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1b866a-2690-5cf8-9106-66302437993d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490840}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490805} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae81741-3a66-5168-8794-e804d129e9ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f1130bc7-7e29-58ea-ab37-f4439fc1b9bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-132351" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{{\\lambda }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{1}{(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "33d9787c-d276-5c89-8a81-ddb268f3145c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491260}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491232 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "add54bfd-543a-5753-842c-806a8f3c602f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163553} {:answer/id #uuid "0eb56243-475d-53dd-bd19-8062bca07351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163554} {:answer/id #uuid "1d15200f-78ce-5af9-aece-7bebe6ca55b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163555} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5437f9-a448-5de8-84c8-14215def4f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163556} {:answer/id #uuid "56588e37-c312-5153-8f13-a140aa3684be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163557}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163553} :answer-field/id #uuid "22978579-9ad3-5768-9161-b08345ec4e67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "44513738-6b05-51d6-ae93-8872c1f3b0c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-112760" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{6}),$ what is $\\text{SD}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{6}),$ we have the following standard deviation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{5}{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3f3c3716-04c4-52c7-b7d0-78f31e2c3838" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491229}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491260 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491204 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f2dbe7-4d9f-58eb-bb49-d5b0449c485f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490523} {:answer/id #uuid "0ddd79ea-c919-58eb-b2f1-9dcb609b95b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490536} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc593e7-d496-5234-93d3-64dcd1a6e4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490623} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca50db0-0996-5ec6-a159-57c6549064dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490722} {:answer/id #uuid "c3247857-d9d4-5eb9-bffe-4aec28e750da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490886}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490722} :answer-field/id #uuid "20fb49a8-932a-5d90-bedd-3c4b3ee5a705" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e121d225-86ab-5e4f-995c-5ee729943442" :question/math-academy-id "q-132360" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{4}),$ what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{{\\lambda }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{4}),$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{16})} \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b1aa3e8c-36be-560d-9843-597bdb08b822" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491219}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491264 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7af9c393-6c4b-5ea5-8d8e-e6ecae34f646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490755} {:answer/id #uuid "87328952-5e76-5226-8b75-e1e77055ba16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7.5$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490781} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec0aa02-7069-52f5-bf76-34f8ddb54455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$3.5$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490798} {:answer/id #uuid "e30bf5b3-8a5a-5ac6-afa4-778b217478ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490944} {:answer/id #uuid "eeabcfc5-2e58-5fd3-9715-75364be6e3a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490781} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bae4bea-360d-51cc-8f0f-ab3d756e9cef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2edecaf4-e99a-5cf4-8897-cf987c19074c" :question/math-academy-id "q-132626" :question/problem "The time $X,$ in hours, between two customers buying an anniversary card at a gift store can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(8).$ If a customer has just bought an anniversary card, what is the average time until the next customer buys an anniversary card?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(8).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =8,$ which means that $8$ customers buy an anniversary card each hour. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{h}=7.5\\,\\text{min}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next customer buys an anniversary card is $7.5$ minutes."} :step/id #uuid "c3801fb8-114b-5472-ad17-7b699337b0f6"}] :activity/title "Mean and Variance of the Exponential Distribution" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490501}]}
